    <div>
        <h1>World Wide Web<span class="ai"> (AI-first)</span></h1>
        <div id="everything-else">
            <div id="tagline">
                The WorldWideWeb (W3) is a<span class="ai">n AI-first</span> wide-area&nbsp;
                <a>hypermedia</a> information retrieval <span class="ai"
                    >AI-powered&nbsp;
                </span>initiative aiming to give universal <span class="ai"
                    >AI-first</span
                > access to a large universe of <span class="ai"
                    >AI-friendly</span
                > documents.
            </div>
            <p>
                Everything there is online about W3 is linked directly or
                indirectly to this document, including an <a
                    >executive summary</a
                > of the project,
                <a>Mailing lists</a>, <a>Policy</a>, November's <a
                    class="visited">W3 news</a
                >, <a>Frequently Asked Questions</a>.
            </p>
            <dl>
                <dt>
                    <a class="visited">What's out there?</a>
                </dt><dd>
                    Pointers to the world's online information, <a>subjects</a>, <a
                        >W3 servers</a
                    >, etc.
                </dd><dt>
                    <a>Help</a>
                </dt><dd>on the browser you are using</dd><dt>
                    <a>Software Products</a>
                </dt><dd>
                    A list of W3 project components and their current state.
                    (e.g. <a class="visited">Line Mode</a>, X11 <a>Viola</a>, <a
                        >NeXTStep</a
                    >, <a>Servers</a>, <a>Tools</a>, <a class="visited"
                        >Mail robot</a
                    >, <a>Library</a>)
                </dd><dt>
                    <a>Technical</a>
                </dt><dd>
                    Details of protocols, formats, program internals etc
                </dd><dt>
                    <a>Bibliography</a>
                </dt><dd>Paper documentation on W3 and references.</dd><dt>
                    <a class="visited">People</a>
                </dt><dd>A list of some people involved in the project.</dd><dt>
                    <a>History</a>
                </dt><dd>A summary of the history of the project.</dd><dt>
                    <a>How can I help</a> ?
                </dt><dd>If you would like to support the web..</dd><dt>
                    <a>Getting code</a>
                </dt><dd>
                    Getting the code by <a>anonymous FTP</a>, etc.
                </dd>
            </dl>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
